capex-digestion window is where a genuine demand shortfall would land.\nCONSISTENCY CHECK vs MY CQ5: CQ5 = 28 requires a durably high-bp-vol decade, which my 62% branch-N supplies, and its correlation leg is the same fiscal-dominance regime as C plus the high-premium upper reach of B. C+D = 27 is the macro-regime cousin of CQ5's 28. Coherent.\nRESIDUAL-B AUDIT, adopted from the Auditor and sharpened by Fermi, because B = 60 must not be read as narrative confidence. Of B's 0.604, the cells with NO literal home total ~0.34: (g4,i2) 0.215 — \"stagnation without disinflation\", which a naive reader assigns to D on the growth clause alone — plus (g2,i1) 0.086, which a naive reader assigns to C on the inflation clause alone, plus (g3,i3) 0.024. That is 56% of B and 34% of the whole distribution. A naive literal reader would report roughly A 13 / B 28 / C 27 / D 32; the lock moves ~19pp out of D and ~13pp out of C into B. B is a DRAFTING RESIDUAL, not a forecast of the Bifurcated Barbell narrative. My B sits between the Wave-1 49-55 and Fermi's 63 for two arithmetic reasons: my growth mode is left of 2.0 so little mass reaches A, and my inflation distribution is concentrated in the homeless 2.0-2.7 band. Note also the LOCK ARTEFACT: A's prose clauses \"debt stabilizes via growth\" and \"broad wage gains\" are NON-OPERATIVE under rule 1, so my CQ1 of 10 (broad wage gains very unlikely) and my A of 13 are not in conflict — I flag that rather than hedge against it.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:53.990Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"G7 GDP-weighted 10y sovereign real yield (10y nominal benchmark minus 10y inflation swap / breakeven, computed on the same seven benchmarks) averages between 1.70% and 2.60% in EVERY one of 2030, 2031 and 2032, with no G7 sovereign having adopted explicit yield-curve control, a